## 💡 Top Hackathon Questions (And how to answer them)

### Q1: "Why did you use FastAPI instead of Django or Node.js?"
> **Answer:** *"FastAPI is built natively on top of Python's ASGI standard, meaning it uses asynchronous code (`async/await`) out of the box. This allows it to handle thousands of concurrent requests with extremely low latency, similar to Node.js, while retaining Python's AI-friendly ecosystem. Plus, it auto-generates our API documentation (Swagger UI), saving development time."*

### Q2: "Why React + Vite instead of Next.js?"
> **Answer:** *"Our platform functions primarily as an authenticated dashboard behind a login wall, rather than a public content site requiring SEO. React with Vite provides an incredibly fast Single Page Application (SPA) experience with client-side routing, which is perfect for complex dashboards without the added server-side rendering complexity of Next.js."*

### Q3: "How are you securing user passwords in the database?"
> **Answer:** *"We never store plain text passwords. We hash them using the industry-standard **bcrypt** hashing algorithm with random salts. Even if a hacker dumps the entire database, they cannot reverse-engineer the passwords."*

### Q4: "How does your backend prevent fake payment confirmations?"
> **Answer:** *"We implement Razorpay's **Webhook / Signature Verification** pipeline. When a user pays, Razorpay generates a cryptographic signature. Our backend takes the order details and re-calculates the signature using our private `RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET` in a secure backend environment. If a user tries to mock a successful payment from the browser, the signatures will mismatch and our backend will reject the request."*

### Q5: "Is your app deployable to local or on-premise servers?"
> **Answer:** *"Yes! The backend is fully **Dockerized** and the frontend compiles to static HTML/JS/CSS files. The entire stack can be run on our cloud server (Railway), local developer machines, or on-premise college servers effortlessly."*
